<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pentagon vows to livestream first military execution in decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3380d485d89681f2851bc8c976e23b8e5f2cd163ff19257be41beb65460291e6</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T10:56:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-pentagon-vows-to-livestream-first-military-execution-in-decades" /><summary type="html">The first US military execution in more than 65 years will be livestreamed, announced the Pentagon on Thursday, after Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said it would be "public".
 
Former Army psychiatrist Nidal Hasan opened fire at Fort Hood in Texas in 2009, killing 13 people. His execution will take place at the military base on December 3, 2026.
 
 "The livestreaming of an execution is tantamount to a public execution and would breach the absolute prohibition of torture," the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights said on Friday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hegseth says Fort Hood shooter's military execution will be 'livestreamed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f681a9370d3e88e7df7b626b3a409947dede95bead47bbec2d5809007a03140</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T09:39:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261009-hegseth-says-fort-hood-shooter-s-military-execution-will-be-livestreamed" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 9: US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth announces that the military execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Malik Hasan will be "livestreamed". But first: we look at reactions in Italy after the country's parliament passes a controversial electoral reform that critics say serves to benefit Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni. Plus, ".fart" and ".trump" are among the new domain name applications, as revealed by the US non-profit organisation ICANN.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>New York mayor to ask Trump for ICE withdrawal after agents shoot man in car with child</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88b410a4b8ab0718ecc6dc5d3c95b91f9004891682d37aa5df952ae5337e1033</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T05:21:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-new-york-mayor-calls-for-ice-removal-after-man-shot-with-5-year-old-nearby" /><summary type="html">New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani has said he will ask US President Donald Trump to remove ICE from the city after federal immigration agents on Thursday shot a man in a vehicle with his five-year-old child during an attempted arrest. The 28-year-old survived and is being treated at hospital.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro wins support of third-place candidate in presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aaf6a43c2aea1fe1c4b5ca1a44d7a290c3726feb87df9ac3948e9e48f978916</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T02:34:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-third-place-candidate-lula--1725ac1116b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-third-place-candidate-lula" /><summary type="html">Brazil's right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro secured third-place finisher Augusto Cury's endorsement on Thursday, strengthening his position against incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva ahead of the runoff. Cury won nearly three percent in Sunday's first round. A Datafolha poll put Bolsonaro ahead with 52 percent against Lula's 48 percent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Families reunited as USS Lincoln returns from troubled 10-month deployment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc199076cd0ab47f5570b298f3b8a459d30b70365b29bd01beda4cea2661cba1</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T00:13:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-families-reunited-as-uss-lincoln-comes-home-after-troubled-gulf-deployment--a048e64efea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-families-reunited-as-uss-lincoln-comes-home-after-troubled-gulf-deployment" /><summary type="html">The USS Lincoln docked in California on Thursday ending a record deployment of 265 days of uninterrupted time at sea marked by reports of deteriorating conditions onboard. Crew members were reunited with family they had not seen in nearly a year after their mission was prolonged by the war in Iran.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US files new torture charges against  Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro and wife Cilia Flores</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcf730e186a437efdde3c8afad80856c86881036240811df471cf10cda6cb6a5</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T23:56:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-us-files-new-torture-charges-venezuela-nicolas-maduro-cilia-flores--cb767909dc08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-us-files-new-torture-charges-venezuela-nicolas-maduro-cilia-flores" /><summary type="html">The United States on Thursday charged ousted Venezuelan president Nicolas Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores with conspiracy to commit torture, adding to drug trafficking and firearms charges. Prosecutors allege detainees, including US citizens, suffered waterboarding, rape and beatings. The pair remain in US custody following a January military raid.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Fort Hood shooter’s firing squad execution to be livestreamed, Pentagon says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:118a2bb3e6793f04f511b7b2c5a3bc322b504870313eca82bd4cbb4d3ad898ab</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T22:01:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-fort-hood-shooter-firing-squad-execution-livestreamed-pentagon--59347f674512.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-fort-hood-shooter-firing-squad-execution-livestreamed-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The Pentagon said on Thursday the firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Malik Hasan would be livestreamed on December 3 after Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth vowed to make the execution "public". Hasan was convicted of killing 13 people and injuring 32 in a 2009 shooting at the Texas military base. The UN on Friday condemned the decision as "torture".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>#IAmJaneDoe: A campaign in solidarity with Cornell alleged gang-rape victim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e3da26906e4e64a0a432ae761d095b1b06bd23e47aa0db412b0736315d464d8</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T15:34:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-iamjanedoe-a-campaign-in-solidarity-with-cornell-alleged-gang-rape-victim--f34505628987.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-iamjanedoe-a-campaign-in-solidarity-with-cornell-alleged-gang-rape-victim" /><summary type="html">A wave of videos is spreading across social media under the hashtag #IAmJaneDoe to express solidarity with an anonymous Cornell University student who alleges she was sexually assaulted by several members of a fraternity in 2024.</summary></entry><entry><title>Democratic party sues Trump administration over taxpayer-funded TV 'propaganda'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69a8f51f34312bed22237ffa0e6ce0f44acedc746e2b49afe2488e263cfc9ecd</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T22:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-dnc-sues-trump-administration-taxpayer-funded-tv-ads--49453418d00f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-dnc-sues-trump-administration-taxpayer-funded-tv-ads" /><summary type="html">The Democratic National Committee sued US President Donald Trump’s administration on Wednesday over taxpayer-funded television ads promoting his political message, alleging illegal government propaganda. The lawsuit seeks to halt federal funding for the ads, which have cost more than $12 million to air ahead of November’s midterm elections, according to AdImpact.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands protest Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro, fearing far-right return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de906a6b8bb03cd50d253ae5c3f7e2746f57af7866ea3167c7ea37f36764f78a</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T22:01:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-thousands-protest-flavio-bolsonaro-far-right-brazil--8b12ff6a5062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-thousands-protest-flavio-bolsonaro-far-right-brazil" /><summary type="html">Thousands of people joined a student march in downtown Rio de Janeiro on Wednesday to protest against presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro ahead of Brazil's October 25 presidential runoff. Bolsonaro led Sunday's first-round vote, prompting demonstrators to rally behind incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and oppose the far right's return to power.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>White House promotes 'Trump TV' with AI-altered photo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fcc4c0c2f2cedca5e28fd3be73f616cccf1a4e459f567ad732ef93bc8904fa0</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:45:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/white-house-promotes-trump-tv-with-an-ai-altered-photo--94598b778013.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/white-house-promotes-trump-tv-with-an-ai-altered-photo" /><summary type="html">The White House has promoted "Trump TV" using an AI-altered photo of passengers apparently watching the president's new streaming channel. But the image was originally posted online in February 2023, showing passengers watching the NFL Super Bowl, with one watching the film "Hitch". The original photo was modified using AI to make it appear as if the passengers were watching Trump TV. The post did not discalose that the image had been altered. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>From the Acropolis, Rubio calls on Europe to emerge from ‘slumber’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a15fa1eb3fd3cd8cc52b13cae0882543c2211f74d218d906bbbefd53801cf29</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-rubio-urges-europe-to-follow-trump-s-america-in-pursuit-of-national-power--081193688361.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-rubio-urges-europe-to-follow-trump-s-america-in-pursuit-of-national-power" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Wednesday urged Western nations to return to what he called their civilisational roots and ensure the West "maintains its place at the head of the world" in a speech delivered against the backdrop of the Acropolis in Athens. The top US diplomat called on Europe to follow President Donald Trump's America in choosing the "unapologetic pursuit of national power" over the "global community".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haiti postpones elections indefinitely amid gang violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71e2ab94620de6109e093740ed19c9e5ef9ea78e8b6b01c44c7ccecac615285e</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T01:06:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-haiti-postpones-elections-indefinitely-as-gang-violence-hampers-preparations--5b2d007ae0d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261007-haiti-postpones-elections-indefinitely-as-gang-violence-hampers-preparations" /><summary type="html">Haiti has indefinitely postponed elections scheduled for December and February, the electoral council said Tuesday, citing technical and operational requirements as gang violence continues to disrupt preparations. The delay leaves Haitians without a democratic process as authorities struggle to register voters and secure areas needed for the poll.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Christa Pike 'angry and confused' after surviving Tennessee execution attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39e85be04b70d858e71a63f7db0e0d48081d69de2b3f66ddbe95567f59cbc5a4</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T23:30:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-christa-pike-regains-consciousness-after-botched-tennessee-execution-attempt--3a4cc81d90d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-christa-pike-regains-consciousness-after-botched-tennessee-execution-attempt" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike is "angry and confused" after regaining consciousness almost six days after Tennessee's failed attempt to execute her by lethal injection, one of her attorneys said Wednesday. Pike, the first woman the state has attempted to put to death in 200 years, remains hospitalised with severe injuries to both arms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Colossal failure: Death penalty system in America is a broken process from start to finish'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1688366480d0fa2edb2262658d658fc7e5357837e958558e445506697bb9c243</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish--4aeddd5f6ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Reed Brody, international human rights lawyer and former New York assistant attorney general. According to Brody, the botched execution of Christa Pike reflects a much larger problem: the relationship between capital punishment, institutional failure, due process, and human dignity. The technical failure of lethal injection exposes weaknesses throughout the legal architecture surrounding the death penalty, from the quality and adequacy of defense representation to the profound disparities between jurisdictions and the difficulties states face in administering executions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f2d9f2f9bff7d241c49196baca9de823ff328a817278bb7ede7bed0b3c42c00</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:05:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says--0d01da482669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35e1dd5547fc0c48f07a9e74cef3f289d0c39757e0751858967c039dc9969215</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:03:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says--155757afd4f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".</summary></entry><entry><title>Paramount completes takeover of Warner Bros, creating media behemoth Skydance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5eee863fdfe8683394ff3614439aa9c905421937f2198612f1844cadfed5be26</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:23:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-paramount-completes-takeover-of-warner-bros-creating-media-behemoth-skydance--ef54048f63ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-paramount-completes-takeover-of-warner-bros-creating-media-behemoth-skydance" /><summary type="html">Paramount completed its acquisition of Warner Bros Discover on Tuesday, after a bidding war against Netflix. The deal closed following federal approval of a settlement between Paramount and 12 US states that tried to block the transaction on antitrust grounds. Opponents in the movie industry warned of job cuts, while media groups said Warner-owned CNN's independence could be compromised.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'They Stole a City' author Lauren Collins on how Wilmington coup was 'covered up'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcd3c07ffe4e6b278779d2da8eafca7080ccba2eea7bffa7eb636e2bcf30b249</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261006-they-stole-a-city-author-lauren-collins-on-how-wilmington-coup-was-covered-up--81dea464a477.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261006-they-stole-a-city-author-lauren-collins-on-how-wilmington-coup-was-covered-up" /><summary type="html">The author of a new book that tells the story of a White supremacist coup in her hometown of Wilmington, North Carolina has spoken to FRANCE 24 about how those involved and the authorities covered up the event for years. The coup happened back in 1898, but was never mentioned in local schools even when she was a pupil. Lauren Collins is currently living in Paris, where she is a staff journalist for The New Yorker. She spoke to us in Perspective about her book, "They Stole a City".</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Mexico makes push for fracking despite environmental concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caf681fd9157b2d7b6f3b980f73b3faa48d4a82e87b151fdd59792881bec32a6</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T12:55:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261006-mexico-makes-push-for-fracking-despite-environmental-concerns--40d4a9cbfcf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261006-mexico-makes-push-for-fracking-despite-environmental-concerns" /><summary type="html">Following months of consultations with energy experts, Mexico is preparing to tap its shale oil and gas reserves using one of the world's most controversial extraction techniques: fracking. The process is already used to extract oil in the southeastern state of Veracruz, where local communities have long complained of pollution and environmental damage. But the administration of President Claudia Sheinbaum is seeking to reduce Mexico's reliance on the United States and – eventually – achieve energy self-sufficiency. FRANCE 24's Quentin Duval and Laurence Cuvillier report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Trump targets tax-free diesel as Republicans approach midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3922507d9628cbf03ac48b07fa61cd458282951738ce3795ca90263114e0d271</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T03:08:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-targets-tax-free-diesel-as-republicans-approach-midterms--32be17b93388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-targets-tax-free-diesel-as-republicans-approach-midterms" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Monday signed an executive order to ease limits on tax-free red-dyed diesel as fuel prices put pressure on Republican candidates. Trump said the move would save farmers millions of dollars and lower the cost of goods, though analysts said the change would not benefit farmers already using tax-exempt fuel.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US to execute 2009 Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan by firing squad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c853ffc697b8d024baad38fa9e63f1b2961c3ff2d4594f732854719f0d79b02</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T01:31:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-approves-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-nidal-hasan--e67cc0cf0a56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-trump-approves-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-nidal-hasan" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump approved a firing squad execution on Monday for Nidal Hasan, the US Army psychiatrist convicted of killing 13 people at Fort Hood in 2009. Hasan's execution will be the first carried out by the US military since 1961, with the date and location yet to be set by the Army.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Quebec votes as separatist surge poses test for Canada PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2af087b95c7607268ac9954f004af9579ca3d3a2f703fc88b9a3a357f2727add</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:36:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/quebec-votes-as-separatist-surge-poses-test-for-canada-pm--438982eb3074.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/quebec-votes-as-separatist-surge-poses-test-for-canada-pm" /><summary type="html">Quebec separatists eyed a return to power in Canada's majority French-speaking province Monday in an election that could test Prime Minister Mark Carney's message of national unity to confront the United States. Carney is popular in Quebec, and the possible success of the separatist Parti Quebecois (PQ) is not seen as a repudiation of his stance toward President Donald Trump, whose trade war and annexation threats have infuriated Canadians. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>New York declares statewide disaster emergency as measles cases rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c58c32524d44bc626ac7fe471f897f1a52d567b4bfbcdbf33e2b81f875f7daaf</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-new-york-declares-statewide-disaster-emergency-as-measles-cases-rise--535ca35f113f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-new-york-declares-statewide-disaster-emergency-as-measles-cases-rise" /><summary type="html">New York Governor Kathy Hochul declared a statewide disaster emergency on Monday as a measles outbreak spreads through under-immunised rural communities, with 108 cases reported this year. The order expands who can administer MMR vaccines and comes as neighbouring Pennsylvania battles an outbreak that has killed five people.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Concerns of US interference weigh on Brazil vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a94edb46ea15ea495710736414d552a9452354c04f9f56c0175f1db988d70cfc</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T20:37:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/concerns-of-us-interference-weigh-on-brazil-vote--868141281be7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/concerns-of-us-interference-weigh-on-brazil-vote" /><summary type="html">Conservative Senator Flavio Bolsonaro pulled off a surprise on Sunday in the first round of Brazil’s presidential election by finishing ahead of the incumbent left-wing President Lula, whom he will face in the runoff on October 25. Suspicions of U.S. interference have been hanging over the campaign, even as Donald Trump has never hidden his closeness to the far-right former president Bolsonaro - Flavio’s father - and his animosity toward Lula da Silva. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Return of the Bolsonaros: Why the far-right surge in Brazilian elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b89217b24eb82bd01d585dcbe0ed3d81003205c459e7106d4ed9cc28f2fc71ce</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T18:44:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261005-return-of-the-bolsonaros-why-the-far-right-surge-in-brazilian-elections--907a05e0e477.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261005-return-of-the-bolsonaros-why-the-far-right-surge-in-brazilian-elections" /><summary type="html">Do voters care about attempted coups? Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro is on the cusp of unseating Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in the country's October 25 presidential runoff. Bolsonaro's father was jailed over the Brazilian version of the January 6 storming of the US Capitol. Up and down the ballot, other Bolsonaros have been elected in the first round as the far right surges. Is it about incumbent fatigue? Do Brazilians subscribe to Bolsonaro's "God, Homeland, Family" mantra?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Quebec separatists vow independence vote after provincial election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca0ce5f14310bafa82129e87461ea28508461f9f06aaaf952a611a318e0e2a4d</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T16:08:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-pledge-to-vote-on-leaving-canada--1a6d962e8ede.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-separatists-win-quebec-election-with-pledge-to-vote-on-leaving-canada" /><summary type="html">The separatist Parti Québécois won provincial elections on Monday, but fell just short of enough seats to govern alone in Canada's French-speaking province, Quebec. The victory comes just two weeks ahead of a vote in Alberta, Canada's economic powerhouse, on whether it wants to begin the process of leaving the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>How Lula’s successes in Brazil may have paved the way for his presidential defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba8eca66c031f5d40e7a0df3892147d1cbe9725a2f939948513f05a829277ff3</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:21:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-how-lulas-successes-in-brazil-may-have-paved-the-way-for-his-presidential-defeat--860d2205f908.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-how-lulas-successes-in-brazil-may-have-paved-the-way-for-his-presidential-defeat" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s veteran leftist President Luiz Inacio "Lula" da Silva trailed Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of his far-right predecessor, in the first-round presidential vote on Sunday. Some analysts suggest that the sweeping anti-poverty measures Lula put in place over two decades may have helped give rise to a growing lower-middle class drawn to the far right’s promise to get the government out of people’s lives.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Very bad result for Lula: Bolsonaro is far more effective at speaking to that growing middle class'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c4156c8f6f9c4790acbba26e5a9281423a1a3fae8fe43938b7f3f3ce6ef7cc3</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:54:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/very-bad-result-for-lula-bolsonaro-is-far-more-effective-at-speaking-to-that-growing-middle-class--d643db93c886.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/very-bad-result-for-lula-bolsonaro-is-far-more-effective-at-speaking-to-that-growing-middle-class" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Felipe Krause, the head of Oxford University's Brazilian Studies Programme. Brazil's election reflects a political landscape that has become increasingly polarized, explains Krause. And he describes the current mood as one of “tired polarization: People are just exhausted. They feel that the political class is just kind of offering more of the same". The first round reveals a significant consolidation of the Brazilian right in government. Brazil's expanding middle class is increasingly attracted to entrepreneurialism and individualism, constituencies that "Bolsonarismo" has proved particularly effective at reaching.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil presidential election: 'Bolsonaro being ahead is a surprise,' researcher says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49ce2aefc43a7cc6bc577bda5c5a79611dad7ef134ac323d160987ee978f31f8</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-bolsonaro-being-ahead-is-a-surprise-researcher-says--c5eb6a7de29c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-bolsonaro-being-ahead-is-a-surprise-researcher-says" /><summary type="html">Far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro has pulled off a surprise win in the first round of Brazil’s presidential election. He defied most polls to win with 47 percent, compared to 45 percent for leftist incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula de Silva. We spoke to Thomas Zicman de Barros, a research fellow at CEVIPOF, the political research centre at Sciences Po University, and columnist for our sister radio station RFI. He told us that never before in Brazilian history has a candidate who was behind in the first round then succeeded in the second.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry></feed>
